; claude: compression, from scratch: Huffman codes, DEFLATE (LZ77 +
; Huffman, RFC 1951) and its zlib wrapper (RFC 1950), with their
; checksums, and its gzip wrapper (RFC 1952: .gz files, HTTP's
; Content-Encoding) -- what PNG's pixels are compressed with, and what JPEG's
; Huffman codes share (see notes_images.md, sections 2, 3 and 6); LZW,
; GIF's; PackBits, the Macintosh's run lengths (MacPaint's pictures,
; and the Amiga's ILBM's as ByteRun1); and the pieces of MPEG's bitstreams, a reader of bits most
; significant first (Bits) and fixed code tables (Vlc); and DEFLATE's
; successor, Zstandard (RFC 8878), decoded: Zstd, over Fse (its entropy
; coder, tANS) and Xxhash (its checksum, XXH64). The Web's, Brotli
; (RFC 7932), is a library of its own, brotli/ (its words are data,
; data/brotli_words/). Independent of
; any format, so that audio's may use them as images' and videos' do.
; In the package tiny_libs, as tiny_libs.compression, pure OCaml.
;
; The folders are folders only, the library the same whichever one a
; module sits in: deflate/ (Inflate, Deflate, their wrappers Zlib and
; Gzip, and Adler32, zlib's checksum) and zstd/ (Zstd, with Fse and
; Xxhash, which nothing else uses); here, what several formats share
; (Huffman, Crc32, Bits, Vlc) and the formats of one module (Lzw,
; Packbits). brotli/ and tests/ have stanzas of their own, so each
; says (include_subdirs no).
(include_subdirs unqualified)

(library
 (name compression)
 (public_name tiny_libs.compression)
 (wrapped false)
)
